# Takes shared links from the on-device share sheet, and answers the app's
# recent list, channel state and transport.
#
# Two kinds of host, for two different reasons, which is why this is
# `requires-any:` (one is enough) and not `requires:` (which is an AND):
#
#   observe  a device someone holds — a mic or a dialer is here, which is the
#            same set of hosts that have a share sheet at all. Bound to
#            127.0.0.1: the only client is an app on this same device.
#   origin   the server the app talks to across the tailnet, with
#            MEDIA_SHARE_BIND and MEDIA_SHARE_TOKEN set. The share sheet on
#            the phone posts *here* when the app is paired to a server.
#
# It said `requires: observe` until 12 Nov 2026, which skipped it on every
# server. red5 never noticed because its unit predates roles; a fresh install
# would have come up without the endpoint the app shares and transports
# through, and nothing would have said so. Found while counting red5's units
# for the red2 move (docs/proposals/2026-11-12-fewer-services.md §4e).
requires-any: observe origin
